    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0735" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2600</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-30T11:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1918, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.09 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2711. The Danish Minister at Petrograd has telegraphed to the Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs announcing the appearance of a Bolshevik decree ordering the arrest of
                    all subjects or citizens of the <pb facs="0736" n="662" xml:id="pg662"/>
                    Associated Governments between the ages of 18 and 45. I further learn that the
                    announcements of Bolshevik victories over the Czechoslovaks have been chiefly
                    fabrications and that the early fall of Vyatka and Perm is expected. Copy to
                    London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
